# vendored lwIP

Source: <https://git.savannah.nongnu.org/git/lwip.git>
Tag:    `STABLE-2_2_1_RELEASE`
Commit: `77dcd25a72509eb83f72b033d219b1d40cd8eb95` (tag target)
License: BSD-3-Clause (see `COPYING`)

## What was vendored

- `src/core/` — the TCP/IPv4 core actually compiled by `CMakeLists.txt`:
  `def.c inet_chksum.c init.c ip.c mem.c memp.c netif.c pbuf.c stats.c
  sys.c tcp.c tcp_in.c tcp_out.c timeouts.c`.
- `src/core/ipv4/` — `ip4.c ip4_addr.c ip4_frag.c`.
- `include/` — the complete lwIP header tree (uncompiled, kept whole to
  avoid missing-include churn).
- `port/arch/cc.h` — the iWAN port's compiler abstraction.
- `lwipopts.h` — the iWAN lwIP configuration.

## What was deliberately NOT vendored

- `src/api/` (socket/netconn/tcpip-thread layers: `NO_SYS=1` + raw API).
- `src/core/ipv6/`, `src/netif/` (ppp/ethernet/slip/zepif), `src/apps/`,
  `test/`, `doc/`, `contrib/` — all disabled by `lwipopts.h` or unused.

## Updating

```sh
git clone --depth 1 --branch STABLE-2_2_1_RELEASE \
    https://git.savannah.nongnu.org/git/lwip.git /tmp/lwip
# re-copy the .c files above and include/, update the commit hash here.
```

The source is vendored (committed) rather than a git submodule so CI builds
stay self-contained and never depend on savannah.nongnu.org being reachable
at checkout/build time.
